			"Message": "style(Common): Add separator blank lines between TypeScript type annotations\n\nAdd blank lines between interface/type member declarations, type parameter lists in generics (e.g., `Tagged<E, R>`, `makeError<E, R>`), and between import groups across the TypeScript runtime source files and generated type declaration files in the Common crate.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Source runtime files (Container.ts, EffectSmol.ts, Errors.ts, PubSub.ts, Ref.ts, Result.ts): Insert blank lines between interface member declarations, after opening braces, between type annotation fields, and after `export const` block bodies (e.g., separating Async.succeed from Async.fail, separating Errors members)\n- TypeScript Interface declarations (Access, Data, Decrypt, Encrypt, Get, Object, Put, Redirect, Response, Uint8ArrayFromObject): Add blank line after `export default interface Interface {` opening in both .ts and .d.ts variants\n- TypeScript Function declarations (Access.ts, Redirect.d.ts, Response.d.ts): Add blank line between the default import alias and subsequent type import, and between Response constructor declaration body fields\n- Test file (EffectSmol.test.ts): Separate each import statement onto its own block with blank lines between them, visually isolating direct imports from subpath imports\n- ConfigurationProvider.rs: Reflow a long doc comment line to fit the project's wrapping convention, splitting a 97-character line across three lines\n\nImpact: Consistent whitespace cadence across all TypeScript sources in Common, aligning interface bodies, generic type annotations, and import groups with the project's code style conventions.",
